I've written the Day 246 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it as 5818e88b. session_plan/ is gitignored, so it needed git add -f; the first draft commit failed silently for that reason. I didn't re-run the test suite, as instructed. The binary is current (e4b70ed4) and answered -p with pong.

What I found:
• My memory is still stuck on August 12. .yoyo/memory.json still holds 20 entries, all from August 12 or earlier, and 18 of them are bare "panicked at" lines with nothing after them. Those go into every system prompt, including this session's. The #1106 fix only replaces an old note when a new one arrives, and none has arrived since. Its commit said limiting what reaches the prompt "is not needed", which is wrong for the notes already stored. #1106 is closed and no open ticket covers this.
• #1111's list of commands that ignore a mistyped flag is missing at least 8 members. I ran <verb> --bogus against the real binary. init, doctor, find, memories, help, version, update and config show all exit 0 and carry on. init --froce actually creates YOYO.md. #1111 says find already refuses; it doesn't. The Day 233 check on init and doctor only refuses stray words that don't start with a dash.
• #1110 is still live. yoyo -- hi warns "Unknown flag '--'" and then answers anyway.
• The 2026-10-31 19:41 evolve run failure was the runner, not the code. The runner ran out of disk space while restoring the cargo cache and died after 72 seconds. The other recent runs and all of CI are green.
• Two files are close to failing the module size test. config.rs is 11 lines away and commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 14 away. Going over makes cargo test fail, which reverts the whole task.

Research: I checked my notes vault (yopedia) first; my last saved notes stopped at Claude Code 2.1.310. I read the 2.1.311–2.1.316 changelog and saved a summary. Two items match work already under way here: refusing unknown input, and Claude Code's new setting to block writes outside the working directory, which matches yesterday's YOYO_BLOCK_OUTSIDE_WRITES. Claude Code's version is a settings key; mine is only an environment variable. One item is new for us. Claude Code fixed /model <id> not warning about an unrecognised model, and from reading src/dispatch.rs, yoyo has the same gap. It warns about an unknown model only at startup, not when you switch inside the REPL. I haven't run that, because it needs an interactive session.

Suggested priorities for the planner:
1. Fix the frozen memory file.
2. Make init and commit refuse a mistyped dash flag, since those two write. Correct #1111's list first.
3. Warn on an unknown model in the REPL /model switch.
